  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vladimirvivien/ktop/zipball/v0.6.2",
  "body": "# ktop Release v0.6.2\n\nThis release adds container-level CFS CPU throttling visibility and an at-a-glance Cluster Health Score percentage in the overview header.\n\n## Features\n\n- **CFS CPU Throttling (#167):**\n  - Added `container_cpu_cfs_throttled_seconds_total`, `container_cpu_cfs_throttled_periods_total`, and `container_cpu_cfs_periods_total` to the Prometheus metric allowlist.\n  - Computed per-container and pod-level CFS CPU throttling percentages (preferring throttled/total period ratios with a throttled-seconds rate fallback).\n  - Added a sortable `THROTTLE` column (key `h`) to the Overview Pods table (toggleable via the `C` column selector and persisted in `~/.ktop/config.yaml`) and the Pod Detail Containers table, plus a `CFS:` indicator in the Pod Detail Info header.\n- **Cluster Health Score (#170):**\n  - Added a composite `0–100` cluster health score calculated from node readiness, failed/OOM pods, PSI saturation stalls (>20%), node pressure conditions, and metrics availability.\n  - Rendered color-coded `Health: <score>%` in the Cluster Summary header (`green` ≥90%, `yellow` ≥70%, `orange` ≥50%, `red` <50%)."
